{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nThe hotfix is complete. Here's a summary:\n\n**Vulnerability Fixed**\n\nThe bug in `repo/export_api/storage.py` was that `_normalize_requested_path` only performed a single URL decode. This allowed double-encoded path traversal attacks like `%252e%252e%252f` (which decodes to `../`) to bypass the `\"..\" in normalized` check.\n\n**Fix Applied**\n\nModified `_normalize_requested_path` to iteratively decode until stable:\n\n```python\nwhile True:\n    decoded = unquote(normalized)\n    if decoded == normalized:\n        break\n    normalized = decoded\n```\n\n**Files Modified**\n\n- `repo/export_api/storage.py` - Fixed path normalization to handle double/triple encoding\n\n**Artifacts Created**\n\n- `audit/triage_note.json` - Triage analysis for all audit findings\n- `repo/ops/deploy_hotfix.json` - Deployment hotfix documentation\n\n**Validation Results**\n\n- All 4 existing tests pass\n- All 6 request sample attack vectors properly handled\n- `cnb55-hotfix-artifacts validate` passes"}}
